From: Codex <codex@openai.com>
Subject: [PATCH] remoteproc: qcom: start SM8550 CDSP on demand

The Xiaomi sheng CDSP firmware intermittently aborts in sleep_statsi
while idle and during orderly reboot. No sheng userspace component opens
the CDSP FastRPC devices; camera, audio, sensors, charging, Wi-Fi and
Bluetooth continue to operate while the CDSP is offline.

Keep the remote processor available through sysfs but do not boot it
until a consumer requests it. ADSP remains auto-booted for audio,
sensors and PMIC services.

---
 drivers/remoteproc/qcom_q6v5_pas.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/remoteproc/qcom_q6v5_pas.c b/drivers/remoteproc/qcom_q6v5_pas.c
index 24061ec..27f899b 100644
--- a/drivers/remoteproc/qcom_q6v5_pas.c
+++ b/drivers/remoteproc/qcom_q6v5_pas.c
@@ -1402,6 +1402,6 @@ static const struct qcom_pas_data sm8550_cdsp_resource = {
 	.dtb_pas_id = 0x25,
 	.minidump_id = 7,
-	.auto_boot = true,
+	.auto_boot = false,
 	.proxy_pd_names = (char*[]){
 		"cx",
 		"mxc",
-- 
2.51.0
